The two False lines above are floating-point ties, not a coding error. At pr=.5 the default's weight can exactly equal the rivals' total, and `int(vote > 0.5)` then resolves the tie by rounding. Rerun (seeds 60000-60003 x 2):
  eps .2 pr .37 and eps .13 pr .61, unreliable, swap10, alternate: fsbma h=0 and mix s7 both identical to bma, lives exactly (efficiencies equal to all digits).
  eps .2 pr .5: identical in swap10; alternate bma 1.667, fsbma/mix 2.084, all 8 lives differ; unreliable 1 life of 8 differs.
  So 1b's "one setting" (bma e=.2 pr=.5) has its ties settled by rounding. Measured in lab/stage1c_replicate.py with pr=.5 +- 1e-6.
